ster hand, though they could be drawing or holding a weak pair. Since you are Out of Position and the pot is small, there is little incentive to bloat the pot with a medium-strength hand. Betting might force out worse hands that you are beating or get you called/raised by better hands (like a Jack or a better 9). Checking allows you to realize your equity cheaply and potentially get to a showdown.\n\nReason: With a middle pair and a weak kicker in a limped pot, pot control is the priority. Checking is the standard play to avoid inflating the pot while holding a marginal hand out of position. It allows you to see the river for free if the opponent checks back.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
