aised bet by 428.\nYour valid actions are: [-2 (All-in), -1 (Fold), 0 (Check), 856 (raise the bet), or any value above 856 but lower than your current chips.].\n', 'reasoning': '**My Poker Hand Assessment**\n\nOkay, so the user wants me to play a hand of Texas Hold\'em. Let\'s see what we\'re working with here. We\'re on hand number 5 out of 20.  I\'m down to 19,900 chips.  That\'s just a small blind, right?  The history shows checks so no bets or calls so far this hand.  But I *thought* I started with 20,000, so where did those 100 chips go? Hmm... let\'s check... Oh, yeah, it looks like this is *just* the current hand\'s information.  Alright, and the user said "Everyone starts with 20,000 chips each hand". Good, that makes things simpler for now.  Let\'s see the rest of the game state.\n\n\n', 'output': "Evaluation:\nThe current game state puts me on the River with a pair of Nines (9d in hand, 9c on board). The community cards are 3d, Jd, 9c, 7h, 5s. There are no flush or straight possibilities for me, and the board is relatively uncoordinated, though a straight is possible for the opponent (e.g., 6-8 or 4-6). The opponent has checked through the Flop and Turn but bets 428 on the River. This sudden aggression on the end suggests either a bluff, a value bet with a better pair (like Jacks or a higher kicker), or a slow-played monster (like a set or straight). My pair of Nines is a weak bluff-catcher at best. I have a weak kicker (2h), meaning any other 9 beats me, as does any pair of Jacks, overpairs (QQ, KK, AA), or two pair combinations.\n\nReason:\nThe opponent's line of checking the flop and turn followed by a river bet represents strength or a polarized range. My hand (middle pair with the worst possible kicker) is too weak to call a significant bet, as I only beat a complete bluff. Given the passive play earlier, a fold is the safest and most statistically sound option to preserve chips for a better spot.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
