uge loss. So the move is: check.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: My hand is 7h 6s on a board of Kh 9s 9d. This is a very weak hand (7 high) with almost zero potential for improvement (no flush draw, very distant straight possibility). The board contains a pair of 9s and a King, which connects well with a wide range of hands that would check pre-flop (like K-x or random 9s). There is almost no equity here. Since no bet has been made in the current round, checking allows me to see the next card for free or give up the hand without losing more chips. Bluffing is ill-advised as the opponent is likely to call with any piece of the board, and the pot is minimal (200 chips).\n\nReason: The hand has no showdown value and very little draw equity. Preserving chips for a better opportunity is the optimal strategy. Checking is the free option.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
